  "prefLabel": "Lab 206.02 Appeal to Supreme Court",
  "priorExpiration": "2007-01-11",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Lab 206.02 Appeal to Supreme Court. Within 30 calendar days after the application for a rehearing is denied, or, if the application is granted, then within 30 calendar days after the decision on such rehearing, the party aggrieved by an order may appeal by petition to the supreme court pursuant to RSA 281-A:43, I(c) and the rules of the supreme court of the state of New Hampshire.\n\nSource. #5041, eff 1-9-91; ss by #5235, eff 9-27-91, EXPIRED: 9-27-97\n\nNew. #6631, INTERIM, eff 11-16-97, EXPIRED: 3-16-98\n\nNew. #6806, eff 7-18-98 (formerly Lab 206.04); ss by #8682, INTERIM, eff 7-15-06, EXPIRED: 1-11-07\n\nNew. #8922-A, eff 7-1-07; ss by #14534, eff 3-12-26 (formerly Lab 206.05)",
